# The only rule here, deliberately.
#
# There used to be 200 rewrites mapping /notes/<id> onto a shell page. They
# caused a redirect loop in production: the shell lived inside the namespace it
# caught, so /notes/detail matched /notes/* and rewrote to itself. Ordering
# exceptions around it would also have swallowed /notes/ask and /notes/admin,
# and would have needed a new exception every time a page was added under
# /notes — a rule that breaks silently, later, when nobody remembers it.
#
# _redirects is a flat first-match list, not a router. Deep links now carry the
# id in a query parameter instead, so there is no rewrite behaviour left to get
# wrong. See docs/STATIC-AUTH-OFFLOAD.md.
/submit-music https://deejaytools.com/ 301
